1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,360
Boxing has been practised for centuries – it was even one of the sports in the original Olympic Games in ancient Greece.
拳击运动已经存在了几个世纪——它甚至是古希腊首届奥运会的比赛项目之一。

2
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:21,630
More recently, boxing has become mainstream in the UK, with hundreds of thousands of people from all walks of life participating in the sport every week.
近年来，拳击在英国成为了主流运动，每周都有数十万来自各行各业的人参与其中。

3
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:23,320
But why?
但这是为什么呢？

4
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:31,140
The answer lies in the physical, mental and even social benefits boxing can bring.
答案就藏在拳击能带来的身体、心理乃至社交层面的益处之中。

5
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:35,070
Its physical benefits are clear.
拳击对身体的益处显而易见。

6
00:00:35,070 --> 00:00:48,760
Whether it’s practising with a punching bag, sparring with a partner or facing an opponent in the ring, boxing can be an intense form of exercise and give a full-body workout.
无论是击打沙袋练习、和搭档进行对练，还是在拳台上直面对手，拳击都是一种高强度的运动，能带来全身锻炼的效果。

7
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:59,440
It can improve muscular strength, and it can also increase anaerobic fitness – allowing someone to work out harder, for longer.
它可以增强肌肉力量，还能提升无氧耐力——让人能够更努力、更持久地运动。

8
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:10,440
These can, in turn, have a positive impact on other aspects of physical well-being, like heart health and weight management.
而这些益处反过来又会对身体健康的其他方面产生积极影响，比如心脏健康和体重管理。

9
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:22,740
But the high physical demands of the sport aren’t just good for the body – boxing can also have a positive impact on someone’s mental well-being.
但这项运动对身体的高强度要求，带来的好处可不止于体魄——拳击同样能对人的心理健康产生积极作用。

10
00:01:22,740 --> 00:01:36,200
Dr Jessica Pinchbeck, Senior Lecturer in Sport and Fitness at the Open University, says that boxing ‘can alleviate some of the symptoms of anxiety and depression’.
开放大学运动与健康专业高级讲师杰西卡·平奇贝克博士表示，拳击“能够缓解焦虑和抑郁的部分症状”。

11
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:47,080
Exercising regularly is already widely known to be good for mental health, but boxing can also bring a sense of discipline and focus.
规律运动对心理健康有益，这早已是共识，但拳击还能培养人自律和专注的品质。

12
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:52,460
And there is a third benefit to putting on the boxing gloves.
戴上拳击手套，还能收获第三种益处。

13
00:01:52,460 --> 00:02:06,220
Practising punches can be done alone, of course, but boxing is not just an individual activity – it also involves working with others to train and stay safe.
击打练习固然可以独自进行，但拳击并非单纯的个人运动——它还需要和他人协作训练，以确保安全。

14
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:18,990
Dr Gavin Williams, Senior Lecturer in Education at the Open University, says that this cooperation and teamwork can ‘create a sense of identity… and belonging’.
开放大学教育学高级讲师加文·威廉姆斯博士称，这种协作与团队精神能够“塑造认同感……和归属感”。

15
00:02:18,990 --> 00:02:30,910
So, no matter what the reason that attracts someone to boxing, the interactive elements of the sport, mean it can also have profound social benefits.
因此，无论人们被拳击吸引的初衷是什么，这项运动的互动属性都能让它带来深远的社交益处。

16
00:02:30,910 --> 00:02:36,340
Good for body, mind and social interactions?
对身体、心理和社交都有好处？

17
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:41,170
It’s not surprising that more and more people are stepping into the ring.
越来越多的人踏上拳台，也就不足为奇了。
